# WeCooked mobile — public runtime configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env and adjust for your machine. .env is gitignored.
# ONLY EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the app, and they are bundled into
# the shipped app — treat everything here as public. Never put a secret
# (API key, OAuth client secret, DB URI, JWT signing secret) in this file.

# --- Backend REST API -------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the WeCooked API (apps/api). The app appends "/api/v1" itself,
# so either form works:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:5000
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.50:5000/api/v1
#
# When this is unset, the app falls back to a local default per platform:
#   - iOS simulator / web : http://localhost:5000
#   - Android emulator     : http://10.0.2.2:5000   (emulator alias for the host)
#
# A PHYSICAL phone can reach NEITHER default — "localhost" on the phone is the
# phone, not your laptop. Point it at your computer's LAN address (shown in the
# Expo CLI output, or `ipconfig` / `ifconfig`), make sure apps/api is listening
# on that interface, and that your firewall allows the port. Phone and computer
# must be on the same network.
#
# The API URL is not a secret. It is only listed here so non-default setups
# (physical device, staging) can override it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# --- Google sign-in (B4.2A source foundation / B4.2B-1 build tooling) -----
# B4.2A shipped the CREDENTIAL-FREE source foundation only: a local native
# module, the login orchestration, and tests. B4.2B-1 adds the build TOOLING
# foundation (expo-dev-client + eas.json development profiles) but still does
# NOT configure Google Cloud, create credentials, log into EAS, or produce a
# native build. Leave BOTH variables below unset for now — the app builds and
# runs, and the Google button reports "not available" safely (Expo Go has no
# native module).
#
# These are BUILD-TIME ONLY and are consumed by app.config.js -> the
# wecooked-google-signin config plugin. They are deliberately NOT prefixed
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ and are NEVER placed under Expo `extra` — JS/runtime never sees
# them. Set BOTH or NEITHER (setting exactly one fails config resolution).
#
# There is NO client secret here. Google verification is server-side (B4.1).
#
#   GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID   Web/server OAuth client ID. Becomes the ID token
#                          audience the WeCooked backend verifies, the iOS
#                          GIDServerClientID, and an Android string resource.
#   GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID   iOS OAuth client ID. Becomes iOS GIDClientID and the
#                          reversed-client URL scheme.
#
# Android's own OAuth client is associated later in Google Cloud (B4.2B-2) via
# com.wecooked.app + the EAS Android signing-certificate SHA-1 — nothing to set
# here for it.
#
# For local config-time use, copy these into .env. For development builds,
# B4.2B-2 will supply the real values to EAS through the EAS "development"
# environment (eas env), NOT through a committed file — .env.example stays
# placeholder-only.
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
